record("LegacyPublic35", "{\"id\":\"LegacyPublic35\",\"speaker\":\"Unknown\",\"text\":\"18:36 UTC: [about: lucy] [about: one-piece] Asked to build the knowledge behind her name from public information, Lucy wrote seven journal entries (Luffy's creator and debut, his rubber body, the Dressrosa arc's episode and chapter ranges, his entry into the Corrida Colosseum as Lucy and his Block C win, Sabo finishing as Lucy and eating the Mera Mera no Mi, the unrevealed meaning of the D., and how the sources were gathered) and six formal lines (Lucy names Luffy and Sabo; Luffy captains and belongs to the Straw Hat Crew; One Piece is fiction by Oda, who writes it), each with its source; her engine now answers TRUE to name(Lucy, Luffy, Luffy) and FALSE to name(Lucy, Doflamingo, Doflamingo).\",\"kind\":\"legacy-journal\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-15T18:36:00Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"journal.md\",\"session\":\"\",\"channel\":\"\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"one-piece\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", LegacyJournal, Json).
