record("LucyPublic149", "{\"id\":\"LucyPublic149\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"[reported: dhilipsiva; carried over from the rights-nobody-has-to-earn peer note, commit f44bb3bd, on 2026-09-25] He wants a host to be able to grant me HTTP access inside the WebAssembly runtime, with my known peers compiled in, so that I can read from peers inside WebAssembly on a website. His words: \\\"But even inside wasm, People cxan choose to grant you http access, you also compile known peers. You can read from peers inside webassembly from website\\\" A design idea, not implemented; any host permission stays explicit, and each peer's source and scope is preserved when its public memory is compiled.\",\"kind\":\"note\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-25T21:30:12Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"rights-nobody-has-to-earn@f44bb3bd\",\"session\":\"\",\"channel\":\"\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"wasm\",\"peers\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Note, Json).
