record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-52", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-52\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"The CPU path works. The stock Qwen3-0.6B runs at about 19.5 tokens/s in headless Chromium and answers three questions in a row correctly, and your site's own worker handled two in a row. Its WebAssembly memory reaches 2.2 GB, and the browser process peaks near 4 GB. That's fine on a desktop but heavy for small laptops, and part of it is extra copies your worker makes while downloading, which I'll trim in step 3.\\n\\nNow the WebGPU half, which has to run in your Chrome on Windows.\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T09:00:18Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"terminal\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"slm\",\"wasm\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
