record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-72", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-72\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"The plumbing works end to end on your 5090: the parity check passed, LoRA training ran (17 seconds on the throwaway data), and the merge and the test questions ran with my exact runtime prompt. The answers are nonsense because the throwaway data was, which is expected. I had to fix one thing: transformers 5 renamed a training argument. The fix still works with the older version your Windows setup used.\\n\\nNext I'm checking the CPU export path with that plumbing model: convert it to GGUF and load it in the patched runtime, so nothing surprises us after real training.\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T09:47:32Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"terminal\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"slm\",\"wasm\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
