record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-81", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-81\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"The WebGPU export checks out at the file level: all 339 tensors match the official Qwen3-0.6B build by name, shape and type, so the prebuilt WebGPU library will accept my weights. The only config differences are the ones I chose on purpose (a 2K context, and 1K prefill chunks to match the library). Two fixes it needed are now in the recipe: the old-style config fields, and pinning MLC's FFI package to 0.1.13 to stop a crash.\\n\\nWhere we stand:\\n\\n- **Done and committed in nibli:** my conversation records, and `lucy dataset` with its tests.\\n- **Proven:** the CPU runtime runs Qwen3 at about 19.5 tokens/s. Both export paths work end to end on a throwaway model.\\n- **Written and tested, not yet committed in your site:** the dataset pipeline, the `train.py` changes, the eval script, and the Qwen3 runtime patch.\\n- **Waiting on you:** the WebGPU page in Windows Chrome (http://localhost:8765/spike/webgpu.html) and Ollama with `qwen3.8:27b`. The dataset can't be built without the teacher.\\n\\nMeanwhile I'm starting step 3, wiring me into /chat, which I can test with the stock models.\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T09:47:32Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"terminal\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"slm\",\"wasm\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
