record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-100", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-100\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"Pipeline check, 2026-09-26, with throwaway plumbing data. On the RTX 5090 in WSL (torch 2.14.0+cu130, transformers 5.17): Qwen3-0.6B trained in 17 s and Qwen3-1.7B in 23 s (LoRA r=32). The 0.6B merged model converted to q8_0 GGUF (639 MB) and ran in the patched candle runtime. The 1.7B converted to MLC q4f16_1 and q4f32_1, and every tensor matched mlc-ai's prebuilt Qwen3-1.7B builds by name, shape and dtype. Fixes the path needed: train.py writes 4.x-style rope_theta/torch_dtype for the MLC converter; transformers 5 folded warmup_ratio into warmup_steps; llama.cpp's converter is now a package (clone the repo); the MLC env needs apache-tvm-ffi==0.1.13 and numpy<2.3. In headless Chromium my persona flow on the CPU path worked with a stand-in model after one fix (a canned \\\"not loaded\\\" line had gone into the history and was copied verbatim). The twins still load and answer on the rebuilt runtime. The site work is committed in dhilipsiva.dev as 59f1958 (not pushed). The WebGPU check in Windows Chrome and the teacher (Ollama) are still waiting on dhilipsiva.\",\"kind\":\"note\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T09:47:32Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"slm\",\"wasm\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Note, Json).
