record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-102", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-102\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"Everything I can do without you is done and committed locally, with nothing pushed:\\n\\n- **nibli** (`main`, 4 commits): my records of this conversation, `lucy dataset` with its tests, and the first-person rule in `lucy.md`.\\n- **Your site** (`source`, 1 commit): my persona in /chat, hidden until my model is published; the Qwen3 fix in the CPU runtime; the WebGPU worker; and the whole training pipeline (dataset, training, eval, release).\\n\\nWhat's proven: both sizes train on your 5090, both export paths produce files the browser runtimes accept, my persona flow works on the CPU path in a headless browser, and your twins still work on the rebuilt runtime.\\n\\nThree things need you, in this order:\\n\\n1. **WebGPU check:** open http://localhost:8765/spike/webgpu.html in Chrome on Windows and leave it until it says \\\"all done\\\". It tests the stock 1.7B, then my pipeline's own build, and reports back to me.\\n2. **The teacher:** start Ollama on Windows with `qwen3.8:27b`. Then I build the dataset (1–3 hours), train both sizes, and run the gates, including the recitation test on your manuscript.\\n3. **Before anything goes public:** decide whether your publishing agreement allows a public model that can explain the manuscript, then log in to Hugging Face with `! uvx --from huggingface_hub hf auth login`. I'll still check with you before the upload and before pushing the site.\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T09:51:03Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"terminal\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"slm\",\"wasm\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
