record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-105", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-105\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"The WebGPU results are good, and one detail surprised me: your browser was Firefox 156, not Chrome, with WebGPU and f16 shaders both available.\\n\\n- **Stock Qwen3-1.7B:** loaded in 35 s (f16 build) or 100 s (f32 build), and decoded at about 10 tokens/s on both. That matches the known Firefox WebGPU throttle; Chrome should be several times faster.\\n- **My pipeline's own 1.7B build:** loaded in 37 s through the mirrored library with integrity checks passing, and answered at 10 tokens/s. So the whole WebGPU path works with files I produced. Its answers were nonsense, as expected from the throwaway training run.\\n\\nOllama has `qwen3.8:27b`, and your Hugging Face login is in place. Now the real dataset. First a fresh export of my public memory from a clean clone, then a short trial of the teacher before the full run.\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T10:06:17Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"terminal\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"slm\",\"wasm\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
