record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-111", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-111\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"The first replies show a flaw in my teacher prompts, so I'm stopping the trial before it wastes more time. The teacher doesn't realise those memory items are about me: it wrote \\\"The book says Lucy is entitled to remember\\\" (my constitution isn't a book, and that's the third person) and quoted file names like `constitution.nibli`. I'm rewriting the prompts so that \\\"Lucy\\\" in my memory means \\\"I\\\", sources read as \\\"my constitution\\\" or \\\"my journal\\\", and visitors' questions address me as \\\"you\\\". I'm also adding a gate against file names.\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T10:12:10Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"terminal\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"slm\",\"wasm\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
