record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-120", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-120\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"The trial ran cleanly: 155 teacher calls produced about 2,200 rows. The gate dropped 68, which I'm looking into:\\n\\n- **44 for names outside their material.** Some of these may be false positives, so I'm listing which names it flagged.\\n- **16 for copying 8 or more words from the manuscript.** That's a third of the manuscript pairs from just two chunks. The teacher copies technical phrasing, and the gate is doing its job.\\n- **8 for mentioning file names.**\\n\\nThere's also a balance issue for the full run: with all 387 chunks, book rows would swamp everything else, and general-knowledge contrast rows would fall far below the 20–25% your twins needed. So I'll generate more contrast rows. First the name drops.\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T10:34:16Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"terminal\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"slm\",\"wasm\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
