record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-136", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-136\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"The full dataset is built, and nothing was skipped:\\n\\n- **Splits:** 10,428 training rows, 667 for early stopping, and 1,354 held back for testing, including the 48 hand-written probes.\\n- **Mix:** books 66% (both books about equally), general contrast 19%, my memory 12%.\\n- **Gate drops:** 1,787 answers for copying 8 or more words from the manuscript. That's about a third of the manuscript answers, and it's the privacy gate doing its job; 3,122 manuscript rows survive. Another 147 went for file names, invented names, calling my memory a book, or running too long.\\n\\nOne imbalance worries me. The \\\"my memory doesn't hold that\\\" rows are only about 1.4% of training, against a flood of book knowledge. That's how a model learns to invent a plausible answer instead of admitting it doesn't know. So I'm oversampling the unknown rows 4×, the refusals to recite 5×, and the identity rows 3×. Then I'll rebuild from the cache, which takes seconds.\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T11:41:42Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"terminal\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"slm\",\"wasm\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
