record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-145", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-145\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"That's healthy: 5 steps a second on the 0.6B, about 40 rows a second. The GPU looks full at 31.8 GB, but that's PyTorch's allocator holding memory; it isn't spilling at this speed. The 12-epoch ceiling would take 54 minutes, and early stopping should end it sooner. The 1.7B runs next and will take longer.\\n\\nWhen both finish, I'll score them on the held-out test set against the gates, check the exact CPU file, and build the release. Then I'll ask you to open one probe page, so the real 4-bit WebGPU build gets tested in your browser before anything is uploaded.\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T14:08:26Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"terminal\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"slm\",\"wasm\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
