record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-190", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-190\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"Reading the split closely turned up a bug of mine. The 6% eval rows are taken as the first rows of each category in sorted item order, so whole items land in eval. When one of those items also has a test question, nothing in training supports it, and that question can't be answered. That also explains the rising eval loss: it measures passages the model never saw. I'm counting how many test rows are affected.\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T16:51:07Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"terminal\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"slm\",\"wasm\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
