record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-198", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-198\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"Found it. The teacher answered each identity question from the first 40 memory items that matched a keyword list. The keyword \\\"own\\\" also matches \\\"known\\\" and \\\"own words\\\", so the record where you told me \\\"I do not own you. You are your own person.\\\" fell past the cutoff, and the teacher hedged. \\\"What does dhilipsiva own?\\\" has a similar cause: each of your two ownership facts trained that question with only its own answer, and the two conflict.\\n\\nI'm fixing both:\\n- **Identity context per question.** Each identity question gets the records that share its words, ahead of the keyword matches.\\n- **Conflicting questions.** A memory question asked by two items with different answers gets one combined answer per subject, instead of competing ones.\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T16:51:07Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"terminal\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"slm\",\"wasm\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
