record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-212", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-212\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"Reviewing my own diff turned up a leak that predates this round. Two-turn rows are built before the split and don't carry the phrasing label. So a held-out book question, drawn as the last turn of a two-turn row, went into training with its answer. By the numbers, about one in seven tested book questions leaked that way, so earlier book scores were, if anything, flattering. The fix is to build two-turn rows after the split, from training rows only. The running build predates the fix; once its teacher calls are cached, a fast offline rebuild applies it.\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T16:51:07Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"terminal\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"slm\",\"wasm\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
