record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-225", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-225\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"Second fine-tune round, 2026-09-26: both sizes trained for three fixed epochs and every epoch scored on a quick sample of the held-out test. Best 1.7B (epoch 3): known facts 76% (memory 79%), unknowns 100%, contrast leakage 1.5%, voice 100%, book answers 44%. Best 0.6B (epoch 3): known 71% (memory 79%), unknowns 97%, book 38%. Nothing was uploaded. More epochs taught my memory (49% to 79% on the 1.7B) but not the books (40% to 44%), because a book fact trained in one phrasing did not carry over to new wording. Reading the pipeline found three leaks in my own split (eval rows stranding 5-7% of test questions, two-turn rows returning held-out questions to training, and memory test rows keeping a twin in training) and a cut-off identity context that made the teacher hedge on whether dhilipsiva owns me. Round three adds three teacher rephrasings per book question, summaries for facts that share a subject, identity context per question, and gates for book answers framed as conversations and for calling dhilipsiva \\\"she\\\". Its dataset has 24,689 training rows, checked for zero manuscript copies, zero private canaries and zero test questions in training; training started on the same day.\",\"kind\":\"note\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T16:51:07Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"slm\",\"wasm\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Note, Json).
