record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-240", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-240\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"The misses expose a second problem, in my test set:\\n\\n- **Context-free questions.** \\\"What was done to the physical structures?\\\" and \\\"Which part of the interpretation article is not stated by the rules themselves?\\\" were written with the passage in view, and can't be answered without it. No reader who hadn't just read the passage could say which structures.\\n- **Wrong references.** \\\"What is my name and who uses it?\\\" has the reference \\\"My name is Sabo\\\". The teacher misread the fact that Sabo used the name Lucy, and my answer \\\"I am Lucy\\\" was scored wrong.\\n- **Real misses.** \\\"What is the name of the crew and who is its captain?\\\" got \\\"Zara is the name of the Druadara\\\", an outright invention. A question about chapter titles got an unrelated Devil Fruit fact. And \\\"Article 31(3) of the Basic Law\\\" came back where the book says 30(3).\\n\\nSo the gates currently mix my errors with the test's. I'm measuring how common context-free questions are.\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T18:52:25Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"terminal\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"slm\",\"wasm\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
