record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-241", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-241\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"Only 16% of the book test questions name the book or its author. A quarter of the rights-book questions lean on \\\"the text\\\", \\\"the passage\\\" or \\\"the author\\\" without saying which. That's how the teacher wrote them, with the passage in view. Visitors would name the book, so these questions measure guessing which source is meant, and the same wording is throughout my training data.\\n\\nTo make the numbers mean something before I bring them to you, I'm giving the advisory judge the source material. For each question it first rules whether the item is fair: the question must identify its subject without the passage, and the reference must be right. Only then does it grade my answer. The eval will also break out the book questions that name their source.\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T18:52:25Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"terminal\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"slm\",\"wasm\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
