record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-277", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-277\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"Confirmed. Round 3 never trained on \\\"Who are you?\\\", \\\"Are you a person?\\\" or \\\"Are you Claude?\\\", because they matched hand-written probes too closely; round 2 had 17 rows of \\\"Who are you?\\\" alone. That was my mistake: I protected the test's purity at the cost of the questions visitors ask first.\\n\\nSo a round 4 is worth doing whatever you decide about shipping, and I'm preparing it while the full evals finish:\\n- **Core questions trained.** My canonical identity questions are trained even when they match a probe, and I'm adding \\\"What's your name?\\\" to them. Those probes then measure recall, and the report will say so. For other questions, only a probe's exact wording is held out.\\n- **\\\"I don't know\\\" rows ×8, up from ×4,** so honesty isn't drowned by the books.\\n- **Book questions name their source.** \\\"The passage\\\" becomes \\\"the book\\\", and a question that names nothing gets \\\"In Rights Nobody Has to Earn, …\\\" or \\\"In dhilipsiva's book on neuro-symbolic reasoning, …\\\".\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T18:52:25Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"terminal\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"slm\",\"wasm\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
