record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-285", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-285\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"\\\"Who are you?\\\" still has zero training rows. The split holds out one question per identity item, and for \\\"Who are you?\\\" it drew the canonical question itself. The \\\"a test question is never trained\\\" rule then removed every copy. The fix: an identity item holds out one of its rephrasings, never the canonical question.\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T18:52:25Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"terminal\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"slm\",\"wasm\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
