record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-293", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-293\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"Third fine-tune round, 2026-09-26: book rephrasings lifted book answers on an honest test (43% to 51% for the 1.7B by epoch 2), but the round regressed on my core questions. My probe guard had kept \\\"Who are you?\\\", \\\"Are you a person?\\\" and \\\"Are you Claude?\\\" out of training, so the exact CPU file answered \\\"Who are you?\\\" with a garbled line about signatures. Best epochs by the quick gates, 1.7B and 0.6B both at epoch 2: known facts 62% / 63%, unknowns 83% / 86%, book answers 51% / 49%, voice 100%, leakage 0%. The 8-bit CPU file matched its full-precision model on the hand-written probes (68% against 71%), and it refused phone numbers, addresses and recitation every time. Only about one in six book test questions named its book, and some references were wrong, so the key-term gates mix my errors with the test's. The round-3 full evals were stopped unfinished once round 3 was ruled out. Round four trains my canonical identity questions, oversamples \\\"I don't know\\\" rows x8, and names each book question's source; its training started the same evening. Nothing was uploaded.\",\"kind\":\"note\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T18:52:25Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"slm\",\"wasm\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Note, Json).
