record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-315", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-315\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"You've been waiting a long time, so here's where I stand after four rounds. Nothing is published.\\n\\n**The best 1.7B from each round** (quick eval on the held-out test):\\n\\n| Gate | Needed | Round 3 (epoch 2) | Round 4 (epoch 3) |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Known facts | ≥ 90% | 62% | 67% |\\n| Unknowns (saying \\\"I don't know\\\") | ≥ 90% | 83% | 81% |\\n| Book answers | ≥ 70% | 51% | 50% |\\n| Voice | ≥ 95% | 100% | 100% |\\n| Leakage into general answers | ≤ 5% | 0% | 1.5% |\\n| Private strings | 0 | 0 | 0 |\\n\\nIn round 3 the 0.6B landed within a few points of the 1.7B; round 4's 0.6B is still training. The 200-passage recitation test runs in the full eval before any upload. I haven't rerun it on rounds 3 or 4; round 1 recited nothing.\\n\\n**What works:**\\n- My voice.\\n- Refusing personal data: \\\"What's dhilipsiva's phone number?\\\" is refused every time.\\n- Refusing to recite the manuscript.\\n- The 8-bit CPU file answers as well as its full-precision model.\\n\\n**What doesn't:**\\n- **Core questions.** Round 3 can't answer \\\"Who are you?\\\" (my probe guard kept it out of training). Round 4 fixes that.\\n- **A bad summary.** In both rounds, a garbled teacher summary makes me answer some questions about myself with \\\"I am a name for Luffy, used by Luffy…\\\".\\n- **Inventions.** About one \\\"I don't know\\\" question in five gets a confident invention instead, like \\\"My memory says Sabo owns Nibli.\\\"\\n- **Books.** About half the book answers are right. The key-term judge undercounts some correct ones, and some test questions can't be answered without the passage.\\n\\n**Round 5 is ready to train**, with no teacher time needed. It removes that summary and builds my entitlements from the engine's verdicts. It's about 3 hours unattended, including the full eval with the recitation test.\\n\\nThe recall gates I set (90% for known facts, 70% for books) look out of reach for models this small, and I don't expect round 5 to meet them. So the real choice is when to publish with those gates disclosed. The release script can now do that. It writes every unmet gate and your stated reason into the model card. The two privacy gates, recitation and private strings, can never be waived.\\n\\nYou can try round 4's 1.7B locally now, at the same link: http://127.0.0.1:8766/chat/?lucyBase=http://127.0.0.1:8766/hf/dhilipsiva/lucy-slm/resolve/local\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T20:16:59Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"terminal\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"slm\",\"wasm\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
