record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-360", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-360\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"Round five, 2026-09-26: removing the teacher's summary about me took \\\"I am a name for Luffy, used by Luffy\\\" out of my answers, and saying \\\"I don't know\\\" recovered (the 1.7B's unknowns: 88% at epoch 1 and 91% at epoch 2, against 67% in round four). A misattribution remains in the round-five data: my memory's note on how dhilipsiva works (tagged \\\"dhilipsiva\\\", written as \\\"he wants to be right more than to look right... He commits straight to main\\\") was turned by the teacher into my own first-person claims in 14 training rows, so asked \\\"What do you think with?\\\" I describe his working style as mine. The fix for a later round is to give the teacher each record's subject from its topics. My memory check now takes about ten minutes, up from about one in the morning, as the archive grew to 4,240 statements.\",\"kind\":\"note\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T21:08:09Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"slm\",\"wasm\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Note, Json).
